// Distributed NATIVE-GATHER schedule — 4 compute workers row-band
// partition the outer `i` axis of the SpMV gather loop. Host runs
// load/save. TASK-0373 (broaden of TASK-0341.03.01 single-worker
// native gather + TASK-0341.03.02 masked distributed).
//
// Drives `prog.gather.algo.nuc` (the native data-dependent-read SpMV)
// rather than the masked `prog.algo.nuc` that `distributed.sched.nuc`
// drives. The DIFFERENCE from the masked distributed schedule is where
// the data-dependent index lives:
//   - masked variant: `x` is read by `x[j]` (iv-affine), the gather is
//     emulated by a `for j` mask in the kernel body — so the halo /
//     transfer passes see only iv-affine indices.
//   - gather variant (this file): `x` is read by `x[col_idx[i][k]]` —
//     the index is a runtime data read at the IndexExpr surface. Under
//     a partitioned schedule this used to be fail-loud rejected
//     (halo_inference's DataDependentStride was fatal under any
//     partitioned scope). TASK-0373 relaxes that to the conservative
//     WHOLE-ARRAY BROADCAST of `x`: every worker receives all of `x`,
//     so any column index it loads is in range.
//
// Partition shape
// ---------------
// `loop i : partition=workers;` on the outermost axis. M=8, 4 workers,
// exact-divisible into 2-row bands (0..2, 2..4, 4..6, 6..8). Each
// worker computes y[i_band] using val[i_band][full k],
// col_idx[i_band][full k], the WHOLE of x, and writes y[i_band].
//
// Per-data transfer mapping (TASK-0301 axis-mapping filter + TASK-0373
// opaque-index rule)
//   - val[i][k]            — i-tiled on tile (filter retains i)
//   - col_idx[i][k]        — i-tiled on tile (filter retains i); the
//                            index ARRAY is itself iv-affine, so it
//                            i-bands like val (TASK-0373 AC#4: col_idx
//                            reaches every worker for its row band).
//   - x[col_idx[i][k]]     — the OUTER array x is indexed by a runtime
//                            data value, NOT by i; TASK-0373 records
//                            that dim OPAQUE (empty iv set) so
//                            compute_partition_bounds_with_dim_prefix
//                            returns whole-array → x is broadcast whole.
//   - y[i]                 — i-tiled on gather (filter retains i)
//
// Why this is bit-identical with naive/gather single-worker
// ---------------------------------------------------------
// Each y[i] is the SAME sum over (k) of val[i][k]*x[col_idx[i][k]]
// regardless of which worker computes it. Workers are independent on i;
// no cross-row carry, no reduction across i. Whole-array x guarantees
// every loaded column index is readable on every worker. The existing
// reference.bin oracle applies — no new reference is needed.
//
// Why sync transfers
// ------------------
// Sync-only schedule lowers on every tier-1 backend that supports
// `sync` (pthreads-sync, mp-tcp-bufsync, mp-tcp-poll, openmp-rs).
// Async-capable backends (pthreads-async, mp-tcp-event, mp-uds-event)
// host this same sync schedule by capability-match on sync; same shape
// as 07-matmul/distributed and 17-spmv/distributed (masked).

schedule for "../prog.gather.algo.nuc" {
    workers = { host, w0, w1, w2, w3 };

    place load_val     on host;
    place load_col_idx on host;
    place load_x       on host;
    place save_y       on host;
    place gather_madd  on { w0, w1, w2, w3 };

    // Row-band partition the outer i axis. M=8, 4 workers ⇒ 2 rows
    // each, exact-divisible (no TASK-0262 floor-with-spillover
    // remainder).
    loop i : partition=workers;

    // All sync transfers. val + col_idx are i-banded by the
    // axis-mapping filter (i appears in their leading index); x is
    // whole-array broadcast (its index is a data-dependent gather, so
    // TASK-0373 records the dim opaque → empty tile bounds → broadcast);
    // y is i-banded on gather.
    transfer val     : sync;
    transfer col_idx : sync;
    transfer x       : sync;
    transfer y       : sync;
}
